<header><p class="enc-kicker">Work / monument · text</p><h1 class="enc-title">Codex Diplomaticus Cajetanus</h1></header>
<div class="enc-body"><p class="enc-desc">The Codex Diplomaticus Cajetanus is a collection of medieval charters from <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/gaeta">Gaeta</a> and its district, published by the monks of <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/monte-cassino">Monte Cassino</a> from 1887. Its documents, beginning in the 9th century, are the main source for the society, economy and rulers of the Duchy of Gaeta, including the family of Docibilis.</p></div>
